GUATEMALA BLOODY COUP, 1982.

@grok, concise, no spin.

300 foreign military and security advisers infiltrated and were suddenly operating in the country.

Foreign press and authorities reported these advisers helped TRAIN, PLAN AND EXECUTE THE COUP alongside militias.

The new dictator, Efraín Ríos Montt, openly credited his soldiers’ foreign training for the coup’s success.

THEN CAME THE MASSACRES.

Within ten weeks, the army slaughtered thousands of unarmed civilians in at least 64 massacres for resisting.

Entire indigenous communities were wiped out, burned and slaughtered.

@grok, which foreign country trained the 300 soldiers and was reported to have helped execute the coup?

@grok country ONLY.
